# License selection source

Choose one supported SPDX identifier and copy the complete corresponding bundled asset to the
target repository's `LICENSE` file. This source file is not copied as `LICENSE`; applying a plan
never fetches license text from the network.

| SPDX identifier | Bundled asset | Apply-time substitution |
|---|---|---|
| `MIT` | `assets/governance/licenses/MIT.txt` | Replace `<year>` and `<copyright holders>` with the accepted year and copyright holder. |
| `Apache-2.0` | `assets/governance/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt` | Replace `[yyyy]` and `[name of copyright owner]` in the appendix with the accepted year and copyright holder. |
| `MPL-2.0` | `assets/governance/licenses/MPL-2.0.txt` | Copy byte for byte; no substitution is required by the license text. |
| `AGPL-3.0-only` | `assets/governance/licenses/AGPL-3.0-only.txt` | Copy byte for byte; no substitution is required by the license text. |

Record the selected SPDX identifier and copyright holder in the plan. Copy only the exact mapped
asset and perform only the substitution listed above; do not replace the license text with a URL,
a summary, or an unresolved token.
